---
description: Ban inline arrow handlers in JSX (onPress, renderItem, etc.)
globs: src/**/*.{tsx,jsx}
alwaysApply: false
---

# No inline render handlers

Do **not** create new functions inside JSX:

```tsx
// bad
<MyButton onPress={() => doThing(id)} />
<FlatList renderItem={({ item }) => <Row item={item} />} />

// good
const handlePress = useCallback(() => doThing(id), [id])
const renderItem = useCallback(({ item }) => <Row item={item} />, [])
<MyButton onPress={handlePress} />
<FlatList renderItem={renderItem} />
```

Allowed:

- Passing a stable reference: `onPress={handlePress}`
- Passing a `useState` setter: `onChangeText={setValue}`
- Reanimated worklet bodies
- `setState(prev => …)` **inside** an already-defined callback (not as a JSX prop expression)
